      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ULTIMATE CRUZA (5) turned in an uncharacteristically poor run most recently when 30 metres away in sixth over 1609m at Newcastle. Left punching into the pace out wide there so we can be forgiving. Same draw this time and he would love a softer run to be at his best but he has the ability to knock this lot off. TOMAHAWK BART (1) was far from disgraced at his latest appearance over 1609m at Menangle, beaten just 1.2 metres into fourth. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. Beautifully placed and looms as a big threat. FIRE FOX NZ (10) is the next best after finishing third over 1720m at this track last time out while BLACK ONYX (11) is worth plenty of thought off a last-start win by 8 metres at this track over 1720m.",
